WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.787
Identify, explain and apply the important ideas behind ram and rom.

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:10.481
RAM: is temporary working memory used while programs run. ROM: stores instructions

00:00:10.481 --> 00:00:13.318
that normally remain when power is off.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.205
Storage: keeps files for later use. Flash drive: is portable file storage. Hard

00:00:19.205 --> 00:00:22.669
drive: is a storage device used in many computers.

00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:28.682
In a small group, draw or safely examine pictures of ram, rom and storage. Explain

00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:31.085
one real-life use for each in Ghana.
